{
  "text": "2003B06 List the potential\nclinical uses of an alpha-2 adrenoceptor agonist\nand outline the limitations of clonidine for each.\nCNS:\nPremedication\n·\nSlow onset (30 mins)\n·\nLong duration (3-7 hours)\n·\nVariable duration (CYP2D6\npolymorphism)\n·\nNo amnesia\nGeneral anaesthesia\n·\nPartial agonist -> ceiling effect,\ninsufficient as sole agent\n·\nProlonged hypotension\n·\nDelayed emergence\nSystemic analgesia\n·\nSedation unwanted\n·\nRebound agitation and hypertension with\nprolonged use\no\nRequires weaning\nNeuraxial analgesia\n·\nProlonged blockade -> inability to monitor\nmotor function\nCVS:\nReflex suppressant\n·\nProlonged effect may be unwanted\no\nLaryngoscopy\no\nSurgery\n·\nUnable to titrate – bolus cf.\ninfusion\nMyocardial ischaemia\n·\nHypotension impairs myocardial oxygen\nsupply\nOpioid withdrawal\n·\nDoes not prevent psychological\ncraving\nEssential hypertension\n·\nα\n2\nadrenoceptor upregulation\n– not for prolonged use\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
